==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|remarkable|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈmɑɹkəbli/|a=GenAm}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈmɑːkəbli/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-remarkably.ogg|a=US}}
* {{hyph|en|re|mark|a|bly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# {{lb|en|manner}} In a [[remarkable]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|He performed the piece '''remarkably''', offering novel interpretations to its nearly cliched passages.}}
# {{lb|en|degree}} To a [[noteworthy]] extent.
#: {{ux|en|That dog is '''remarkably''' fierce.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-04-09|author=Andrei Lankov|title=Stay Cool. Call North Korea’s Bluff.|work=w:The New York Times|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/opinion/stay-cool-call-north-koreas-bluff.html?_r=0
|passage=Suggestions that those leaders are irrational and their decisions unfathomable are '''remarkably''' shallow. North Korea is not a theocracy led by zealots who preach the rewards of the afterlife.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20130411070140/http://www.nytimes.com/2013/04/10/opinion/stay-cool-call-north-koreas-bluff.html|archivedate=2013-04-11}}
# {{lb|en|evaluative}} {{non-gloss|Used to draw special attention to a proposition}}.
#: {{ux|en|'''Remarkably''', three State assembly elections were decided by a total of fewer than one hundred votes.}}

